TAM-VT-SCREENSHOT

tam-vt-screenshot captures the active Linux virtual console framebuffer
(/dev/fb0) as an opaque RGB PNG and writes it to ~/Pictures/vt-<timestamp>-<tty>.png
under the UID/GID of the active VT's owner (or the primary normal user when a
VT is at a root-owned login prompt).

Invoked by tam-vt-screenshot.service via kbrequest.target when PrtSc is pressed
on a text console (mapped by tam-vt-keymap.service).
